<item><title>Togo, Benin and Ivory Coast sign accord to coordinate LNG supplies</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/tg/togo-benin-and-ivory-coast-sign-accord-to-coordinate-lng-6031db/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/tg/togo-benin-and-ivory-coast-sign-accord-to-coordinate-lng-6031db/</guid><category>Togo</category><description>The agreement also plans cross-border gas infrastructure as Togo studies a port terminal, with no final decision announced.</description><pubDate>Thu, 26 Nov 2026 08:26:58 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/tg.jpg" length="29610" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/tg.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Lomé airport cancels Royal Air Maroc flight after technical incident</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/tg/lome-airport-cancels-royal-air-maroc-flight-after-technical-9d1077/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/tg/lome-airport-cancels-royal-air-maroc-flight-after-technical-9d1077/</guid><category>Togo</category><description>The service to Casablanca was cancelled on 24 November, and 111 passengers were accommodated in a local hotel while new-aircraft routing began.</description><pubDate>Thu, 26 Nov 2026 00:00:18 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/tg.jpg" length="29610" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/tg.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Gnassingbé seeks opposition backing for possible 2027 early elections</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/tg/gnassingbe-seeks-opposition-backing-for-possible-2027-early-77fd47/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/tg/gnassingbe-seeks-opposition-backing-for-possible-2027-early-77fd47/</guid><category>Togo</category><description>Togo’s government is trying to unite a divided opposition behind early legislative polls after an ECOWAS court ruling on the country’s republic.</description><pubDate>Wed, 25 Nov 2026 19:02:07 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/tg.jpg" length="29610" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/tg.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Togo proposes 2 684,1 milliards of FCFA budget for 2027</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/tg/togo-proposes-2-684-1-milliards-of-fcfa-budget-for-2027-a79ab5/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/tg/togo-proposes-2-684-1-milliards-of-fcfa-budget-for-2027-a79ab5/</guid><category>Togo</category><description>The draft is 2,5 % below the 2026 initial budget, while 921,4 milliards of FCFA is set aside for debt service.</description><pubDate>Wed, 25 Nov 2026 12:36:23 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/tg/togo-proposes-2-684-1-milliards-of-fcfa-budget-for-2027-a79ab5/share.jpg" length="39547" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/tg/togo-proposes-2-684-1-milliards-of-fcfa-budget-for-2027-a79ab5/share.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
